\n\nD) Cod eat almost only hairy scale fish, which are also the main food for seals.\n\nThis seems like a strong option. If cod eat only hairy scale fish, and those are the same fish that seals eat, then when there are more seals, they would eat more of that fish, which is also what the cod is relying on. So if the seal population increases, they might be overeating the same fish that cod depend on, leading to a decline in cod. This directly connects the increase in seals to a decrease in cod because they're both consuming the same prey. So this weakens the original argument because it shows that the increase in seals could indeed be affecting the cod population through their shared food source.\n\nSo, putting it all together, option D directly challenges the assumption that the increase in seals doesn't impact cod because it shows that the same food source is being exploited by both, leading to a decline in cod. Therefore, the option is "]]  6%|6         | 37/600 [00:37<09:06,  1.03it/s]
