ditional etiquette. It also mentions sending tea as a way to express nostalgia, using tea as a gift, and other customs like worshiping the Buddha or sacrifices. Additionally, it notes that different ethnic groups have varied tea drinking habits, each with their own beauty.\n\nNow, looking at the options:.\n\nA) Tea culture in ancient poems. The text mentions Du Lei's poem, which is about tea, so this seems relevant.\n\nB) Folk customs related to tea. The text discusses various folk customs like sending tea as a gift, worshiping the Buddha, etc., so this also seems relevant.\n\nC) There are many ways to drink tea and tea art. The text says there are many ways to drink tea and mentions tea art procedures, so this is likely correct.\n\nD) Tea drinking customs in different regions have their own advantages. The text does talk about different ethnic groups having their own habits, but it doesn't explicitly state that these have advantages. It just describes the diversity.\n\nSo, the question is which can be inferred. The text provides examples of various customs and art, so C seems directly supported. It also mentions different regions, which supports D, but the text doesn't say they have advantages, just that they exist. Therefore, the option is "]]
