ting income is. From the context, it's income that doesn't come from the main business or specified ancillary businesses. It's considered net income but not generated by operating activities and doesn't require payment or matching expenses.\n\nLooking at the options:.\n\nOption A: Service company's ticket revenue. Since it's part of the main business, it's operating income, so this is correct.\n\nOption B: Policy subsidy from a different company. Subsidies are usually not part of regular operations, so this should be non-operating. Correct.\n\nOption C: Fines paid by company b to company a. Fines are usually related to regulatory violations and are part of operating expenses, not non-operating income. So this might be incorrect.\n\nOption D: Scrap payment from selling equipment. This is from an asset disposal, which isn't part of regular operations, so it's non-operating. Correct. Therefore, the option is "]]
