o do not cherish time, 24 hours is only 24 hours. This doesn\'t quite fit because the passage doesn\'t specifically talk about valuing time; it\'s more about how time is given.\n\nC) People who cherish their time can make good use of their time. This aligns with the idea that while time is the same for everyone, how we use it depends on our priorities. So, people who value their time use it wisely.\n\nD) In a sense, everyone\'s time is different. This also touches on the idea that even though everyone has the same amount of time, how they use it varies, making it different for each person.\n\nWait, so both C and D seem relevant. The passage is about the paradox of time being both fair and biased. The main point is probably that how we use time is what makes it biased, which is covered in C. D is more about the variation but not the main point of the paradox. Therefore, the option is ']]
