ncorrect assumption. Therefore, the argument requires that the public square's freedom was complete, which is what option C states.\n\nAlternatively, option A is about access. If not everyone has the same access, then the comparison might not hold. But the argument is about freedom of expression, not access. So maybe the main assumption is about the completeness of freedom in the public square, not access.\n\nSo, putting it all together, the argument assumes that the public square's freedom was complete, so the internet should match that. Therefore, the option is "]] 20%|##        | 123/600 [02:14<04:11,  1.90it/s]
