s to be really clean, the detergent must dissolve. The argument assumes that without dissolution, the clothes won't be clean. So, if A is true, then the argument holds. If A were false, maybe a detergent could be clean without dissolving, which would weaken the argument.\n\nOption B is saying that only the special detergent can make the machine clean. The argument does suggest that a special detergent is needed, but it doesn't say that no other detergent can work. So, B might not be necessary because the argument doesn't claim that no other detergent can be used, just that a special one is needed.\n\nTherefore, the assumption required is likely A because it's a necessary link between detergent dissolution and cleanliness. Therefore, the option is "]] 78%|#######8  | 468/600 [08:58<01:36,  1.37it/s]
