s or doesn't weaken the idea that synthetic pesticides are safe because humans are used to natural plant toxins.\n\nLooking at the options:.\n\nA) The concentration of natural drugs in plants is much lower than synthetic pesticides. If the natural drugs are less concentrated, then maybe they aren't as effective. But the argument is about safety, not effectiveness. So if the concentration is lower, it might mean that the natural drugs are less potent, but the argument is about the safety of using synthetic pesticides. So this could undermine the argument because if natural drugs are less effective, they might not protect as well, making synthetic pesticides a safer alternative.\n\nB) Humans have ingested natural drugs for thousands of years and can adapt. This supports the argument because it explains why humans aren't affected, so using synthetic pesticides is safe. So this doesn't undermine the argument; in fact, it strengthens it.\n\nC) Synthetic pesticides have simpler structures. Simpler structures might mean they're less likely to have side effects, but the argument is about the effectiveness of natural drugs versus synthetic ones. So this could support the argument by suggesting that synthetic ones are safer, thus not undermining it.\n\nD) Natural drugs are specific and synthetic are harmful to various organisms. This makes sense because if natural drugs only work on specific parasites, while synthetic ones are broad-spectrum, then synthetic might be safer in a general sense. So this supports the argument, meaning it doesn't undermine it.\n\nSo, the question is which option does NOT undermine the argument. The argument is that synthetic pesticides are safe because natural drugs are effective and humans are familiar with them.\n\nOption A suggests that natural drugs are less concentrated, which might mean they're less effective, potentially making synthetic ones more effective and thus more harmful. So A would undermine the argument.\n\nOption B supports the argument, so it doesn't undermine it.\n\nOption C supports the argument by suggesting synthetic are safer, so it doesn't undermine.\n\nOption D supports the argument by explaining why synthetic are better, so it doesn't undermine. Therefore, the option is "]] 78%|#######8  | 469/600 [08:58<01:22,  1.59it/s]
