h is a form of retraining and starting a new business, but it\'s more about moving into a different field rather than just updating skills.\n\nOption C: It\'s more about personal hobbies and additional skills, not tied to a specific occupation.\n\nOption D: Starting a kindergarten, which is a new venture, but not necessarily tied to professional skills or updating them.\n\nSo, both A and B seem to fit, but the question is which one belongs to professional socialization as per the definition. The definition emphasizes choosing occupations based on social needs, so A is about choosing a new occupation (translation) because of social needs, while B is more about military service and then starting a repair business, which might be a different context.\n\nWait, but in B, he was already in the army, so maybe the social needs were met through the military, and then he expanded into another field. So, both A and B involve choosing a new occupation or expanding skills, but the question is which one fits the definition better.\n\nThe definition says "choose occupations according to social needs," so A is about choosing a new occupation (translation) because of social needs, while B is more about military service and then expanding into another business. So, A is more about aligning with social needs by choosing a new occupation, which fits the definition better. Therefore, the option is ']] 79%|#######8  | 472/600 [09:01<01:46,  1.20it/s]
