messages:  [['Please act as a math teacher and reason step by step to solve the logical reasoning problem. Given a context and a question, explain your reasoning process and give the answer with the format "\\nThe correct option is: A/B/C/D".\n####\n# Context:\nZhao Ming, Qian Hong and Sun Jie were admitted to Peking University, Tsinghua University and Beijing normal University. About which school they were admitted to, the students made the following guesses: classmate A guessed: Zhao Ming was admitted by Tsinghua University and Sun Jie was admitted by Beijing normal University. Classmate B guess: Zhao Ming was admitted by Beijing normal University and Qian Hong was admitted by Tsinghua University. Classmate C guess: Zhao Ming was admitted to Peking University and Sun Jie was admitted to Tsinghua University. As a result, the students\' guesses were half right.\n\n# Question:\nBased on the above information, which of the following options is their correct admission?\n# Options:\nA) Zhao ming, qian hong and sun jie were admitted to peking university, tsinghua university and beijing normal university respectively.\nB) Zhao ming, qian hong and sun jie were admitted to tsinghua university, beijing normal university and peking university respectively.\nC) Zhao ming, qian hong and sun jie were admitted to beijing normal university, tsinghua university and peking university respectively.\nD) Zhao ming, qian hong and sun jie were admitted to peking university, beijing normal university and tsinghua university respectively.\n\n# Instruction:\n## Reasoning:', ".\nOkay, so I have this logic problem here, and I need to figure out which option correctly shows where Zhao Ming, Qian Hong, and Sun Jie were admitted. Let me try to break this down step by step.\n\nFirst, the context says that each of the three students—Zhao Ming, Qian Hong, and Sun Jie—was admitted to one of three universities: Peking University, Tsinghua University, and Beijing Normal University. Each of their classmates made guesses about where each person was admitted. The key point is that each classmate's guesses were half right. That means for each guess, one part was correct and the other was wrong.\n\nLet me list out the guesses:.\n\n- Classmate A guessed:.\n  - Zhao Ming was admitted by Tsinghua University.\n  - Sun Jie was admitted by Beijing Normal University.\n\n- Classmate B guessed:.\n  - Zhao Ming was admitted by Beijing Normal University.\n  - Qian Hong was admitted by Tsinghua University.\n\n- Classmate C guessed:.\n  - Zhao Ming was admitted to Peking University.\n  - Sun Jie was admitted to Tsinghua University.\n\nSince each classmate's guesses are half right, each of their two statements must have exactly one correct and one incorrect.\n\nLet me start by analyzing each classmate's guesses and see if I can find overlaps or contradictions.\n\nStarting with Classmate A:.\n- A1: Zhao Ming → Tsinghua (maybe correct).\n- A2: Sun Jie → Beijing Normal (maybe correct).\n\nBut since only one is correct, either A1 is correct and A2 is wrong, or A1 is wrong and A2 is correct.\n\nSimilarly for Classmate B:.\n- B1: Zhao Ming → Beijing Normal (maybe correct).\n- B2: Qian Hong → Tsinghua (maybe correct).\n\nAgain, only one is correct.\n\nClassmate C:.\n- C1: Zhao Ming → Peking (maybe correct).\n- C2: Sun Jie → Tsinghua (maybe correct).\n\nOnly one correct.\n\nNow, let's see if we can find contradictions or confirmations.\n\nFirst, let's consider where Zhao Ming is admitted. He's guessed by all three classmates:.\n\n- A1: Tsinghua.\n- B1: Beijing Normal.\n- C1: Peking.\n\nSo Zhao Ming is either Tsinghua, Beijing Normal, or Peking, but only one of these is correct.\n\nLet me assume each possibility and see if it holds.\n\nCase 1: Zhao Ming is Tsinghua (from A1 correct).\n\nIf Zhao Ming is Tsinghua, then:.\n\n- A1 is correct, so A2 must be wrong. So Sun Jie is not Beijing Normal. Therefore, Sun Jie must be either Peking or Tsinghua. But Tsinghua is already taken by Zhao Ming, so Sun Jie must be Peking.\n\nNow, looking at C2: Sun Jie → Tsinghua. Since Sun Jie is Peking, C2 is wrong. Therefore, C1 must be correct. So Zhao Ming is Peking? Wait, no, because we assumed Zhao Ming is Tsinghua. Wait, that's a contradiction because C1 says Zhao Ming is Peking, which would be correct if Zhao Ming is Peking, but we assumed he's Tsinghua. So this case leads to a contradiction because C1 would have to be correct, but we already have A1 correct, so C1 must be wrong, which would mean Zhao Ming is not Peking, but we assumed he is Tsinghua. So this case might not hold.\n\nWait, maybe I made a mistake. Let me re-examine.\n\nIf Zhao Ming is Tsinghua (A1 correct), then A2 is wrong, so Sun Jie is not Beijing Normal. So Sun Jie must be either Peking or Tsinghua. But Tsinghua is taken, so Sun Jie is Peking.\n\nNow, looking at C1: Zhao Ming is Peking. But we assumed Zhao Ming is Tsinghua, so C1 is wrong. Therefore, C2 must be correct. So Sun Jie is Tsinghua. But wait, Sun Jie can't be Tsinghua because we just said Sun Jie is Peking. That's a contradiction. So this case is invalid.\n\nTherefore, Zhao Ming cannot be Tsinghua. So A1 must be wrong, meaning A2 is correct. So Sun Jie is Beijing Normal.\n\nSo now, Sun Jie is Beijing Normal (A2 correct, so A1 wrong).\n\nNow, let's look at B's guesses:.\n\nB1: Zhao Ming → Beijing Normal (but Sun Jie is Beijing Normal, so B1 is wrong. Therefore, B2 must be correct. So Qian Hong is Tsinghua.\n\nNow, Qian Hong is Tsinghua.\n\nNow, let's look at C's guesses:.\n\nC1: Zhao Ming → Peking (unknown yet).\nC2: Sun Jie → Tsinghua (but Sun Jie is Beijing Normal, so C2 is wrong. Therefore, C1 must be correct. So Zhao Ming is Peking.\n\nSo now, we have:.\n\nZhao Ming: Peking.\nQian Hong: Tsinghua.\nSun Jie: Beijing Normal.\n\nLet me check if this fits all the conditions.\n\nChecking A's guesses:.\n- A1: Zhao Ming → Tsinghua (wrong).\n- A2: Sun Jie → Beijing Normal (correct).\nSo A has one correct, one wrong. Good.\n\nChecking B's guesses:.\n- B1: Zhao Ming → Beijing Normal (wrong).\n- B2: Qian Hong → Tsinghua (correct).\nSo B has one correct, one wrong. Good.\n\nChecking C's guesses:.\n- C1: Zhao Ming → Peking (correct).\n- C2: Sun Jie → Tsinghua (wrong).\nSo C has one correct, one wrong. Good.\n\nSo this seems to fit all the conditions. Now, let's look at the options.\n\nOption A: Zhao Ming Peking, Qian Hong Tsinghua, Sun Jie Beijing Normal. That's exactly what we have. So Option A is correct.\n\nWait, but let me check the other options to make sure.\n\nOption B: Zhao Ming Tsinghua, Qian Hong Beijing Normal, Sun Jie Peking. But we determined Sun Jie is Beijing Normal, so this can't be right.\n\nOption C: Zhao Ming Beijing Normal, Qian Hong Tsinghua, Sun Jie Peking. No, because Sun Jie is Beijing Normal.\n\nOption D: Zhao Ming Peking, Qian Hong Beijing Normal, Sun Jie Tsinghua. No, because Sun Jie is Beijing Normal, and Qian Hong is Tsinghua, but Sun Jie can't be Tsinghua. Therefore, the option is "]]
