dia is highlighting these areas, making it seem like crime is worse than it actually is. So this would cast doubt because it's possible that the increase in media coverage is just because people are more aware of their local areas, not because actual crime has increased.\n\nOption A, on the other hand, is about the media's coverage being more comprehensive, which could mean they're reporting more crimes, but it's possible that the number of actual crimes hasn't increased, just that the media is covering more of them. So A could also be a point of doubt.\n\nBut I think C is a stronger argument because it directly relates to the perception of crime being higher by pointing out that people are more aware of their own neighborhoods, leading to more crimes being experienced locally. So the media might be focusing on these areas, making it seem like crime is out of control when it's actually just people being more cautious. Therefore, the option is "]] 96%|#########6| 576/600 [11:57<00:14,  1.64it/s]
